# Required by api/remediate.ts (the live Remediation Agent integration).
# A fine-grained GitHub Personal Access Token scoped to just this repo,
# with Contents: Read and write + Pull requests: Read and write.
# Set as a real secret in Vercel Project Settings -> Environment Variables.
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# Optional: which repo the Remediation Agent targets. Defaults to
# vepopuri/secure_sdlc if unset.
# GITHUB_OWNER=vepopuri
# GITHUB_REPO=secure_sdlc

# Optional: an Anthropic API key. When set, the Remediation Agent calls
# Claude Opus 5 to generate a real root-cause analysis + patch + test
# strategy for the whitelisted finding, instead of writing a static
# template note. Without it, the template note is used — nothing breaks.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional shared-secret gate. If DEMO_TRIGGER_SECRET is set, the server
# rejects any /api/remediate request that doesn't send the same value in
# an x-demo-secret header. VITE_DEMO_TRIGGER_SECRET is the client-side
# copy the frontend build inlines and sends automatically — set BOTH to
# the same value, or leave both unset. This only raises the bar (it ships
# inside the public JS bundle, so treat it as a filter against casual/
# accidental triggering, not real access control) — recommended once this
# app's URL is shared publicly, since anyone with the link could otherwise
# trigger a real GitHub write.
# DEMO_TRIGGER_SECRET=
# VITE_DEMO_TRIGGER_SECRET=
